From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:20:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/apple-dart: Keep the retained MTP and display messages
 board-neutral

The retained MTP bypass and the retained display DARTs are admitted on
more than one T8132 board: the MTP path on the MacBook Air (13-inch, M4)
and the MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4), the display path on the boards listed
in apple_dart_retained_display_boards. Both still announce themselves as
"J713", so a MacBook Pro logs

  apple-dart 394800000.iommu: Retaining the live J713 MTP bypass

which points whoever reads the log at the wrong machine.

Drop the board name from both messages; the machine model is already in
the log. Move the MTP boards into a table, the same way the display
boards are listed, so that admitting another board changes the table and
not the condition. The admission checks themselves are unchanged: the
machine must still be a listed T8132 board, the DART must be the
unlocked, non-tunnelled T8110 at 0x394800000 with bypass support, and
every stream must be in bypass with no valid translation table.

The module parameters and the Kconfig option that carry "j713" in their
names are user-visible and are left alone.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index c3b989594b..7ee43fb49b 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -3929,6 +3929,16 @@ static bool apple_dart_retained_display_board(void)
 	return of_machine_compatible_match(apple_dart_retained_display_boards);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Boards whose loader leaves the MTP (keyboard and trackpad) coprocessor
+ * running with every stream of its T8110 DART at 0x394800000 in bypass.
+ */
+static const char *const apple_dart_retained_mtp_boards[] = {
+	"apple,j713",
+	"apple,j604",
+	NULL
+};
+
 static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	int ret, sid;
@@ -4256,21 +4266,20 @@ params_done:
 	dart->fw_mirror = dart->locked && !dart->fw_handoff &&
 		(of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8140-dart") ||
 		 of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8142-dart"));
-	if ((of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") ||
-	     of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604")) &&
+	if (of_machine_compatible_match(apple_dart_retained_mtp_boards) &&
 	    of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8132") &&
 	    res->start == 0x394800000ULL && dart->hw->type == DART_T8110 &&
 	    !dart->locked && !tunneled && dart->supports_bypass &&
 	    apple_dart_streams_bypassed(dart)) {
 		dart->retained_mtp = true;
-		dev_info(dev, "Retaining the live J713 MTP bypass\n");
+		dev_info(dev, "Retaining the live MTP bypass\n");
 	}
 	if (dart->preserve_display) {
 		if (dart->hw->type != DART_T8110 || !bitmap_empty(dart->remapped, DART_MAX_STREAMS)) {
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 			goto err_clk_disable;
 		}
-		dev_info(dev, "J713 display DART version %04x, locked %d\n",
+		dev_info(dev, "Retained display DART version %04x, locked %d\n",
 			 dart->version, dart->locked);
 		ret = res->start == 0x30a340000ULL ? apple_dart_dcp_prepare(dart) :
 			apple_dart_frontend_prepare(dart);
